sentences.l:
but exceedingly
I feel shame before the Trojans and the Trojan women trailing-robed,
if like a base man apart I shun the war;

And you might, being in Argos, at another woman’s bidding weave the web,
and you might carry water from Messeis or Hypereia,
much against your will, and strong necessity will lie on you;

“Zeus and you other gods, grant indeed that this one too become,
my child, even as I am, outstanding among the Trojans,
so good in strength, and of Ilium to be lord with force;

But going into the house, tend to your own tasks,
the loom and the distaff, and to the handmaids give orders
to ply their work;

So Priam’s son Paris down from high Pergamus,
in his armour all-shining like the sun, had set out,
exulting, and his swift feet bore him;
